# .gitignore
# WHY: Prevents secrets and generated files from being accidentally committed.
# If terraform.tfvars or hosts.ini end up in Git, your AWS access keys
# and server IPs become public – a serious security incident.

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Environment files (may contain secrets)
.env
.env.*

# Terraform state – contains resource IDs and sometimes secrets in plaintext
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Terraform variable overrides – contains YOUR IP and key paths, never commit
terraform/terraform.tfvars

# Ansible dynamic inventory – generated by Terraform with real server IPs
ansible/inventory/hosts.ini

# Ansible retry files
*.retry

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.exe
